---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — Panta"
  description="What panta.llc collects and why: anonymized Google Analytics with your consent, cookieless page counts and speed measurements, contact details you choose to send us, and nothing else."
>
  <section class="section section--dark" style="padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label">Privacy</p>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.2rem);">Plain-spoken, like everything else here.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 46rem;">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        With your consent, we use Google Analytics to understand how visitors
        use this site — pages viewed, rough location (IP addresses are
        anonymized), and how you found us. If you decline, Google Analytics
        never loads.
      </p>
      <p>
        Separately, our host Vercel counts page views for us and measures how
        quickly pages load for you. It sets no cookies, stores nothing on your
        device, and never identifies you or follows you to other sites — so it
        runs for everyone and isn't part of the consent choice above. It tells
        us how many people visited a page and how fast it was, not who they
        were.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you contact us or book a consultation, we receive what you send:
        your name, email, and message. We use it to reply and for nothing
        else. We never sell personal data.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to Pulse, our newsletter, your email address is stored
        by <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">Buttondown</a>,
        our newsletter provider, on servers in the United States. We also record
        the IP address you signed up from as proof of consent. Subscribing takes
        two steps: you enter your address, then click a link in a confirmation
        email — we don't add anyone who doesn't confirm. Every issue has a
        one-click unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing removes you for good. We
        use the address to send Pulse and nothing else, and we never sell it.
      </p>
      <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">Change your mind</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your analytics choice anytime:
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" style="margin-left: 0.5rem;" id="reopen-consent">Update consent</button>
      </p>
      <p class="small" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        Questions? <a href="mailto:hello@panta.llc">hello@panta.llc</a> — we
        reply within one business day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  document.getElementById('reopen-consent')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    try {
      localStorage.removeItem('panta:consent');
    } catch (_) {
      /* swallow */
    }
    document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('panta:consent-reopen'));
  });
</script>
